WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.003
-Today, a federal
communications commission

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.040
voted to repeal the Obama-era
net neutrality rules.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.908
Meanwhile,
the Trump White House

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.110
was once again
consumed by petty dramas.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.012
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:17.650
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.553
Today, the Republican-led FCC
voted to dismantle

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.022
the free and open Internet
by repealing

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.391
former President Obama's
net neutrality rules,

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.194
which were designed to ensure
that all web traffic

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.930
is treated equally
and prevents service providers

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.932
from blocking
or filtering content

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.400
they don't want you to see.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.904
The FCC is led by Ajit Pai,
who is best known

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.239
for both his opposition
to net neutrality

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.775
and for the size
of his coffee mug.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.176
-Greetings, Chairman Pai.

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:45.878
Mindy Hill with TheDCVoice.com.

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:48.948
-Hi.
-And I just have a comment.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:53.253
During the Obama administration,
the FCC had no jurisdiction...

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.286
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.722
...over regulating programming.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:01:01.594
-I'm sorry, but you can't just
drink from a mug that size

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.896
without any explanation.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.129
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.600
Was the mug always that big,
or did you shrink?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.537
Are you sharing an office
with Rick Moranis?

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.272
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.107
Is that why you want
to limit the Internet,

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.243
so people can't go online
and make memes about you

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.078
and your giant coffee mug?

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:23.850
Now, polls show
that Americans overwhelmingly

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.117
support net neutrality,

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:28.020
with 83% overall in favor
of keeping the FCC rules,

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.356
including 75% of Republicans,

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.293
and it makes sense Republicans
would favor an open Internet.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.827
Otherwise, they'd have
to get their news

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.629
from newspapers or CNN

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.432
instead of Facebook group
PatriotEagleMAGA1776.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.733
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.736
Net neutrality ensures an open
and democratic Internet,

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.038
where people can make
and access content equally.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:49.042
But Pai has argued that limiting
regulation of the Internet

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.443
would actually encourage
companies to innovate more,

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:54.180
and he keeps using
one phrase in particular.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.316
-Until 2015,
we had light-touch regulation.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:02:00.419
The consumer is best served
with light-touch regulation.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.954
It's under
that light-touch framework --

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.021
Light-touch regulation --

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.390
Light-touch regulation --

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.392
And that's the kind of success
that we want to promote

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.628
in the future,
with light-touch regulation.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.230
-Please stop using the term
"light touch."

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.600
You sound like someone
defending themselves to HR.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.867
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.669
"What did Deborah say I did?
That was a light touch!"

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:18.704
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:22.107
You were there!
It was light!"

00:02:22.107 --> 00:02:25.945
And yet despite the potentially
disastrous consequences

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.914
of this vote, D.C. and the Trump
White House in particular

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:31.317
have been consumed once again
by chaos and drama,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:35.021
like, for example the firing
of longtime Trump ally Omarosa.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.822
Now, Omarosa's
official job title

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.391
was Communications Director for
the Office of Public Liaison,

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.427
but no one was ever really sure

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.495
exactly what she did
in the White House.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:46.832
In fact, before she was fired,
all anyone had ever heard

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.867
about Omarosa's time
in the White House

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:51.437
was that she held a photo shoot
with her bridesmaids

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.506
there in April
before getting married.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.942
Politico reported
that Omarosa brought members

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:59.279
of her 39-person bridal party
to 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.980
for an extended
wedding photo shoot,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.016
catching fellow senior aides
and some security officials

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.252
by surprise
in her bridal attire.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.254
The visitors
loudly wandered around,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.256
looking to snap photos
in the Rose Garden

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.624
and throughout the West Wing.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.060
Oh, my God. Trump's staff
treats the White House

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.262
the way tourists
treat the M&amp;M Store.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.596
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.832
"I want a picture
with the green one!"

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.366
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:25.104
Also, 39 bridesmaids?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.539
Is it a massive wedding,

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.708
or are you just trying to make
one friend feel really terrible?

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:32.111
"I'm sorry, Becky,
the max was 39,

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.880
and you're my 40th best friend."

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.481
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.583
Now, apparently,
it was Chief of Staff John Kelly

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.952
who did the firing,
although Trump signed off on it,

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.522
reporting that
was confirmed by April Ryan,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:45.358
White House correspondent of
American Urban Radio Networks,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.392
in one especially great moment

00:03:47.392 --> 00:03:50.529
when Ryan called back
to Trump's famous catchphrase.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.864
-So, General Kelly had
had enough,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.400
and he'd finally gotten
the President to sign off.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.369
And last night,
it did not end well.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.971
-She was a contestant
on "The Apprentice,"

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.173
President Trump's
former TV program,

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:03.209
so they have a history.
They go way back.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.777
-And she was fired again.
-Twice, yeah.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.878
-All right.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.479
I don't know if he said,
"You're fired."

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:08.614
-He didn't say, "You're fired,"

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:09.949
but General Kelly said,
"You're fired."

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.617
-All right.
Everybody stand by.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.085
There's more news.

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:16.355
-Damn, look at her sipping from
her mug while she says that.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:17.489
The only way
that would've been better,

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:18.825
if she had Ajit Pai's mug.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.694
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.496
Today on "Good Morning America,"

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.731
Omarosa claimed
that the stories about her exit

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:27.266
from the White House
were not true.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.168
Specifically,
she refuted reports that

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.237
she blew up at Kelly
and had to be escorted

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.538
off the White House premises.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.274
In fact, Omarosa said
that she didn't make a scene

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.910
and that Kelly fired her
in a very private place.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.747
-I resigned, and I didn't
do that in the residence,

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:43.315
as being reported.

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:46.653
John Kelly and I sat down
in the Situation Room,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:50.122
which is a very secure, very
quiet room in the White House.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.757
-Wow, the Situation Room.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.660
Though I have a feeling
any room Omarosa goes into

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.229
becomes a Situation Room.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.597
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.732
Seriously, you know it's bad
when they have to fire you

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.535
in the same place
they killed Osama Bin Laden.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.236
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:05.538
Omarosa --

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:11.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.479
Omarosa also claimed
she had a story to tell

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.047
and would eventually
tell that story

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:16.415
once her tenure
at the White House

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:17.650
is officially over.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.185
And later,
when the "GMA" anchors

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.486
were discussing the interview,

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.389
Robin Roberts gave her
the perfect sendoff.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.791
-She said
she has a story to tell,

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.325
and I'm sure
she'll be selling that story.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.360
-We'll see.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.827
-Yeah, she will.
Bye, Felicia.

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:32.664
-Damn.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:34.900
D-a-a-amn!

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.337
I wish all news anchors
signed off that way.

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:40.439
That's how Edward R. Murrow
should've signed off

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:41.707
during the McCarthy era.

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.776
"Good night, good luck,
and bye, Felicia."

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.177
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.646
Now, of course, it's never fun
to relish anyone's firing,

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:49.849
but Omarosa routinely attacked
Trump's critics

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.584
and even went so far as to
threaten people who crossed him.

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:55.154
And while Robin Roberts
might have been ice-cold,

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:58.324
others were less muted in their
reactions to Omarosa's firing,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.793
like CNN commentator Angela Rye.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.894
-Brooke, I'm gonna do
what you can't do

00:06:02.894 --> 00:06:07.032
and what April and Symone
are too good of people to do,

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:08.601
and that's just
gonna be petty for a minute.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.602
Ahh-ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:10.602
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:11.704
-Oh, Angela.
Oh, Angela.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.606
-Bye, girl!
Bye!

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.075
Goodbye, good riddance, goodbye.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.210
Deuces. Out.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.345
-Angela, you know
I have much love for you,

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.446
but you know what?

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.247
I don't delight
in anyone's demise.

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:23.782
-I'm not delighting
in her demise.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:25.784
I wish her the best,
but ahh-ha-ha!

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:32.892
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:36.696
-I'm not sure you can really
say, "I wish her the best"...

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:37.796
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:39.131
...when it's followed by this.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.234
-Ahh!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:44.069
-When she did that, I'm pretty
sure the closed captioning said,

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.138 line:0%
"I wish her the best -- psych!"

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.773 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:49.708
But, of course,
Omarosa is not the only

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:51.844
longtime Trump acolyte
who's suddenly on the outs.

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:54.547
There's also former White House
Chief Strategist Steve Bannon,

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:57.316
an early and vocal backer
of Roy Moore in Alabama.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.919
Bannon went to war
with the GOP establishment

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.821
and managed to lose
a Senate seat in arguably

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.556
the most Republican state
in the country,

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:06.058
and that has led to many
Republicans turning on him,

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.294
like New York Republican
Congressman Peter King,

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:11.397
who did not hold back in an
interview on CNN on Wednesday.

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:14.300
-Why Bannon?
Why is he such a big deal?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.802
-I was even ready -- not even so
much as a political issue.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.271
Almost as a moral issue.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:20.939
This guy does not belong
on the national stage.

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:22.608
He looks like some
disheveled drunk

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.644
that wandered onto
the political stage.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:28.047
-Hey, Peter King,
you doing my job now?

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:29.248
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:33.085
I'll do the "looks like" jokes
around here.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.620
Steve Bannon looks like a cop

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.656
who went undercover
to solve a case,

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:39.291
and then they forgot to tell him
the case was solved,

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:41.993
so he just stayed undercover
for another 10 years.

00:07:41.993 --> 00:07:46.098
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.434
"I got a lead!"

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.003
So, Republicans on the FCC
are trying to dismantle

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:53.973
the free and open Internet,
despite overwhelming opposition,

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.108
and the Trump White House
is consumed once again

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.376
by petty drama.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:59.245
I don't know how long it'll be
before Republicans

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.380
are kicked out of office,
but when it happens,

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.115
I hope it's reported like this.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.182
-Bye, Felicia.

00:08:04.182 --> 00:08:05.484
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:09.188
[ Cheers and applause ]

